  EucFACE (mature, P-limited)                    --        --        --        --        --        

=== 4. THE CONSTRAINT IS ON THE PAIR, NOT ON beta_max ===
  Read down any column above: a single FACE target fixes beta_max ONLY once
  fert_k is fixed. Read across: the same target is met at beta_max values
  differing several-fold. So a MARGINAL prior on beta_max cannot encode this
  evidence -- it has to enter as a term in the ratio R(a,e), which is a
  JOINT constraint on (beta_max, fert_k). That is also why the uniform
  prior is not merely uninformative: beta_max is not the identified object.

=== 5. THE ACTIONABLE RESULT: FACE PUTS A CEILING ON fert_k ===
  R is NOT monotone in K -- it peaks at an INTERIOR K and falls away on
  both sides (low K saturates the increment; high K inflates the ambient
  denominator). So a high-K cell has a MAXIMUM achievable FACE response
  even at beta_max = 3, and that is what rejects the corner.

  --- ambient 376 -> 530 ppm ---
      fert_k     max R at beta_max=3  reaches 21.8%? 23%? 10%?
       120.0                   28.8%  yes    yes    yes   
       318.0                   36.0%  yes    yes    yes   
       554.5                   33.4%  yes    yes    yes   
      1000.0                   26.4%  yes    yes    yes   
      1500.0                   20.9%  NO     NO     yes   
      1783.7                   18.6%  NO     NO     yes   
      2000.0                   17.1%  NO     NO     yes   
  => fert_k above ~1400 cannot reach the 21.8% synthesis target at ANY
     beta_max in [0, 3]. The pinned probes sit at 1738 and 1784.

  --- ambient 400 -> 564 ppm ---
      fert_k     max R at beta_max=3  reaches 21.8%? 23%? 10%?
       120.0                   23.7%  yes    yes    yes   
       318.0                   31.9%  yes    yes    yes   
       554.5                   31.0%  yes    yes    yes   
      1000.0                   25.6%  yes    yes    yes   
      1500.0                   20.7%  NO     NO     yes   
      1783.7                   18.6%  NO     NO     yes   
      2000.0                   17.3%  NO     NO     yes   
  => fert_k above ~1374 cannot reach the 21.8% synthesis target at ANY
     beta_max in [0, 3]. The pinned probes sit at 1738 and 1784.

=== 6. WHAT IT DOES NOT SAY ===
  * FACE is temperate FOREST NPP. `beta_max` here multiplies GLOBAL NPP,
    which includes grasslands, croplands and the tropics -- where there is
    NO forest FACE experiment at all. This is a prior, not a measurement.
  * The 21.8% synthesis is plantation-weighted; the two MATURE sites are
    the two smallest responses (EucFACE negligible, BIFoR +10%). Using the
    headline alone would repeat the ratio_needs_its_base error.
  * EucFACE's 0% prints as unreachable above only because beta_max = 0 is
    the boundary of the search, not because the model cannot represent it.
  * FACE is a step change over years; `beta_max` is an equilibrium
    asymptote. The mapping assumes the MM form transfers between them.

=== 7. MARCUS 2026-08-25: THE EXACT NUMBERS ARE NOT A CONSTRAINT ===
  Standing instruction: FACE is temperate FOREST, so its VALUES cannot bound a
  global parameter -- but its response SHAPE and its REALISTIC LIMITS can.
  Section 5's fert_k ceiling is a VALUE result, so it has to be re-priced as a
  function of the assumed response rather than quoted at one target.

  --- ambient 376 -> 530 ppm | R peaks at fert_k = 317, box max R = 36.0% ---
  assumed R    K floor   K CEILING   probes 1738/1784
       0.0%       none        none   survive -- NO ceiling in the box
       5.0%       none        none   survive -- NO ceiling in the box
      10.0%         25        none   survive -- NO ceiling in the box
      13.6%         37        none   survive -- NO ceiling in the box
      15.0%         42        none   survive -- NO ceiling in the box
      17.3%         51        1973   survive
      20.0%         63        1600   REFUTED
      21.8%         72        1400   REFUTED
      23.0%         78        1283   REFUTED

  --- ambient 400 -> 564 ppm | R peaks at fert_k = 376, box max R = 32.1% ---
  assumed R    K floor   K CEILING   probes 1738/1784
       0.0%       none        none   survive -- NO ceiling in the box
       5.0%       none        none   survive -- NO ceiling in the box
      10.0%         34        none   survive -- NO ceiling in the box
      13.6%         51        none   survive -- NO ceiling in the box
      15.0%         58        none   survive -- NO ceiling in the box
      17.3%         71        1993   survive
      20.0%         89        1592   REFUTED
      21.8%        103        1374   REFUTED
      23.0%        113        1246   REFUTED

  THE CEILING IS A KNIFE EDGE AT ~17.5 %, AND THE PROBES PREDICT 17.3 %.
  Above ~17.5 % a ceiling exists and cuts the probes off; at 15 % or below there
  is NO ceiling anywhere in [20, 2000]. So section 5's '~1374-1400' is not a
  realistic limit -- it is a restatement of the 21.8 % plantation-weighted
  headline, which is exactly the number Marcus rules out as a constraint.
  SECTION 5's ACTIONABLE RESULT IS WITHDRAWN: option (b), narrowing the fert_k
  bound on the FACE argument, is NOT available on this criterion.

  WHAT SURVIVES AS A SHAPE / LIMIT STATEMENT, target-free:
   S1 R is NON-MONOTONE in fert_k with an INTERIOR peak (317-376 across the
      ambient range) and a BOX MAXIMUM of 32.1-36.0 %. The model structurally
      cannot produce a larger FACE response at ANY point of the prior box. Any
      assumed response below ~15 % is reachable at essentially any fert_k.
   S2 The constraint is on the RIDGE COORDINATE, not on either parameter. In the
      linear regime (K >> 140 ppm) only beta_max/K is identified:
        design (arithmetic, 08-14)   beta_max/K = 0.00409 /ppm  ->  R =   7.8%
        adopted mode (arm N)         beta_max/K = 0.00182 /ppm  ->  R =  13.6%
        pinned foss probe (08-23)    beta_max/K = 0.00155 /ppm  ->  R =  17.3%
        pinned luc probe (08-24c)    beta_max/K = 0.00153 /ppm  ->  R =  17.2%
        the bound itself             beta_max/K = 0.00150 /ppm  ->  R =  17.3%
      Mapping the literature RANGE (0-23 %) onto that coordinate is the honest
      form of the evidence; mapping one target onto fert_k is not.
   S3 EVERY cell above sits INSIDE the literature's 0-23 % span, so on the range
      rather than a point, FACE REFUTES NOTHING. It brackets. The adopted mode's
      13.6 % sits mid-range and nearer the mature-forest end; the probes' 17.3 %
      sits above the mature sites and below the plantation synthesis.

  AND A SHAPE CLAIM THAT IS NOT AVAILABLE, stated so it is not reached for later:
   * Single-elevation FACE cannot identify the CO2 response FORM. Every site is
     one ambient and one elevated level, so it fixes a chord, not a curvature.
   * The mature-vs-young contrast is saturation in STAND AGE and NUTRIENT STATUS,
     not in CO2. Reading it as evidence for MM's CO2 saturation is a category
     error; it is a LEVEL statement about where a global mean should sit.


